  "details": "Spawning as the first joiner may occasionally violently jerk/yeet/throw you around in the world at high velocity until respawn.\n\nReproduction steps:\n\n- Unknown reproduction steps\n\n- The effect reportedly happens rarely\n\n- The effect can happen in the home world right after VRChat starts\n\nObserved:\n\n- The player is violently thrown around in the world at high velocity\n\n- The camera can roll in such a way that the virtual world's horizon will no longer match the real playspace horizon, causing loss of balance\n\n- The player may sometimes bypass the world colliders, going out the normal boundaries of the world\n\n- The effect persists until respawn is triggered by going out Y bounds\n\n- Before the effect happens, the player sometimes spawns outside of the world, or in a location that is not normally a spawn\n\n- This appears to only affect the first joiner of a world (instance master)\n\n- If the user was already in calibrated inside full body tracking, the avatar may be mangled with incorrect IK target positions until the avatar is reset",
